WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.810
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:24.490
Unit 2 · Thinking Like a Computer · done!

3
00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:31.710
Unit 3 · Building With Blocks

4
00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.910
Chapter 1 · Meet Block Coding

5
00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:44.320
Code without typing? Let's find out!

6
00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:52.600
Peeking at Riya didi's laptop…

7
00:00:52.600 --> 00:01:04.140
Typed code: lots of strange words!

8
00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:17.360
One tiny typo → ERROR!

9
00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:28.910
Is there an easier way? Think!

10
00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:35.400
"When I was your age, I started with blocks!"

11
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.380
It's called BLOCK CODING

12
00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:44.080
Snap puzzle-like blocks to give instructions

13
00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:55.460
Drag · Drop · Snap!

14
00:01:55.460 --> 00:02:10.020
No typing, no spelling mistakes!

15
00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:14.700
A block coding screen has 3 parts

16
00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:21.850
Left: the blocks, sorted by colour

17
00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:26.890
Middle: snap your blocks together here

18
00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:40.130
Right: the stage, with Billu the character

19
00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:47.820
A stack of blocks = a PROGRAM

20
00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:55.670
Billu follows it from top to bottom

21
00:02:55.670 --> 00:03:07.310
Just like algorithm steps, in order!

22
00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:13.240
Meet 4 blocks, each with its own job

23
00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:28.760
Start: when green flag clicked · goes on top

24
00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:39.050
Motion: move 10 steps · Billu walks

25
00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:47.020
Wait: wait 1 seconds · a little pause

26
00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:53.510
Say: say Hello! · shows a speech bubble

27
00:03:53.510 --> 00:04:08.270
Flag → Move → Say → Wait → Move

28
00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:12.920
Click the green flag!

29
00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:26.010
Billu follows every block, in order

30
00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:34.130
Is a start block = a motion block?

31
00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:50.420
Start = when to begin · Motion = move

32
00:04:50.420 --> 00:05:10.130
Match each block to its job!

33
00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:24.510
Start · Move · Wait · Say, all matched!

34
00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:42.460
Click the flag… nothing happens! Why?

35
00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:52.700
Missing: the start block on top!

36
00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:56.580
Your turn: practice check

37
00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:06.430
Why blocks first, instead of typing code?

38
00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:25.000
Easy to see & snap · no typos · focus on ideas

39
00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:32.440
Block coding = snap blocks, no typing

40
00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:37.620
Program = a stack, top to bottom

41
00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:41.930
The start block goes on top

42
00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:47.540
Start · Move · Wait · Say: each has a job

43
00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:55.520
Chapter 1 done!

44
00:06:55.520 --> 00:07:02.320
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
